/-! # A kernel-feasible packed Eighth source tensor

The packed tensor of the Eighth axis (worker `gforest`, `eighthSrcVecW w`) is the triality image
`twTriTen w 2048 (srcEighthYX w) (srcEighthYL w).sh.odd`, whose kernel evaluation (a word action and
a long sum of single entries) is memory-heavy.  `eighthSXF w` stores the numerators (over
`8192`) as compact literal columns with `16`-bit fields, re-spaced to width `w` by `respace`;
one cross-sum kernel check at width `88` binds it to the source tensor (`eighthSXF88_ten`), and
`eighthSXF_bnd` gives its tensor bound at every width `w ≥ 16`. -/

